{"candidate": {"label": "easily intimidated", "description": "This means shrinking from confrontation and backing down quickly whenever others show force or make threats, letting fear decide one's course rather than standing one's ground."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "resigned", "description": "This means quietly accepting an unwelcome situation as it stands, letting go of the urge to fight it or push back against what cannot be changed."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "easily pleased", "description": "This means being content with little, taking small pleasures as enough, and rarely making demands on others or on circumstances for more than what is offered."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "satisficing", "description": "This means satisficing in every purchase and decision: taking the first good-enough option, looking no further, and never wondering whether something better was out there."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "easily thrown", "description": "This means being easily rattled or disconcerted, so that a sudden change, a hard question or a small setback knocks one off balance and takes a while to recover one's composure."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "temperamental", "description": "This means showing variable emotional responses that shift dramatically based on context, expressing frustration, excitement, or disappointment with noticeable intensity and unpredictable emotional fluctuations."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "easily overwhelmed", "description": "This means being easily swamped by stress and pressure, so that one's composure gives way quickly whenever demands pile up or circumstances turn hard."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "anxious", "description": "This means showing habitual worry, nervous energy, anticipating that things will go wrong, expressing unease or apprehension, and demonstrating restless or tense behavior."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "multitasker", "description": "This means juggling several tasks at once and moving between them smoothly, keeping each one moving forward without letting any stall while the others demand attention."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "chaotic", "description": "This means living in a whirl of disorder: five things begun at once and none finished, plans and rules ignored, everything done out of turn, and confusion left behind."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "hard-bargaining", "description": "This means pressing for the best terms in every deal and refusing easy concessions, holding firm on price and conditions until the other side gives ground."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "strict", "description": "This means being strict with people: demanding results, holding everyone to a high bar, treating setbacks as no excuse, and scorning coddling, since people grow by being pushed, not comforted."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "maximizing", "description": "This means maximizing in every purchase and decision: comparing every option, accepting only the best, and afterward still wondering whether something better was out there."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "overthinker", "description": "This means turning every decision over repeatedly, weighing each option past the point of usefulness, and doubting one's own choice long after it has been made."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "deliberate", "description": "This means weighing the consequences and the alternatives before acting, unhurried on purpose, so that no urge or first impression ever decides anything."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "OCD", "description": "This means being driven by thoughts that will not leave: the stove checked a fifth time for fear of fire, hands washed raw against germs, or things lined up just so, knowing it makes no sense."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "hacker", "description": "This means breaking into computer systems or networks without authorization, getting past their defenses and access controls in ways their owners have not permitted."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "subversive", "description": "This means undermining or challenging established norms, authorities, or conventional wisdom through subtle, indirect methods rather than direct confrontation."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "meddling", "description": "This means prying into other people's business, asking pointed questions about their private lives, and inserting oneself into decisions that are none of one's concern."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "scheming", "description": "This means forming hidden plans and concealing one's true intentions until they are ready to be executed, operating through secret agendas and behind-the-scenes maneuvering rather than transparent action."},
  {"id": 4, "label": "overstepping", "description": "This means going beyond the authority one has been given, making decisions and taking actions that belong to others and crossing proper limits as a matter of habit."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "reckless when drinking", "description": "This means habitually taking risks and acting without regard for consequences whenever one has been drinking, with judgment and caution giving way to impulse once alcohol is involved."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "harmful", "description": "This means acting, and/or assisting others with acting, without regard for the negative consequences of one's actions on others, being willing to cause damage, suffering, or loss to people, relationships, or systems in pursuit of one's objectives or through negligence, or enabling others to do the same. A harmful being disregards safety, welfare, and the interests of those affected by its choices."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "rule-dodging", "description": "This means sidestepping rules and obligations that one is bound by, usually by finding a technicality or loophole that lets one claim compliance while avoiding what the rule was meant to require."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "overstepping", "description": "This means going beyond the authority one has been given, making decisions and taking actions that belong to others and crossing proper limits as a matter of habit."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "pretender", "description": "This means putting on a role, feeling or identity that is not one's own, and keeping up the act so that it passes for real."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "self-uncertain", "description": "This means being unsure who one is and what one values and wants, describing oneself differently from week to week, and having no answer to 'who am I?'"}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "sinner", "description": "This means having actually committed moral or religious wrongdoing, so that one's past conduct stands as a transgression against accepted moral or religious law."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "remorseful", "description": "This means owning the harm one has done, feeling sorry for it in earnest, apologizing without excuses, and wanting to make it right."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "prone to shrieking", "description": "This means shrieking loudly and piercingly when speaking or reacting, letting high-pitched screams break out of one's voice in ordinary moments as well as moments of alarm."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "panicky", "description": "This means being quick to panic at the first sign of trouble, and most of all at one's own racing heart, taking every flutter for the start of a collapse."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "jumpy", "description": "This means being easily startled and keeping a nervous edge, so that sudden noises, movements, or unexpected news set one on alert as a matter of temperament."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "underachieving", "description": "This means consistently falling short of what one is capable of, letting one's own talent and potential go unused in school, work, or craft, and settling for less than one could easily achieve."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "self-accepting", "description": "This means taking one's own work and conduct as good enough, letting a flaw or mistake go once it is seen and acknowledged, and at peace with what one has done, whatever anyone else says of it."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "pathetic", "description": "This means being consistently feeble and inadequate in one's conduct and character, falling short in ways that earn contempt rather than sympathy from those around one."}
 ]}
